API-21: SCOTCH_graphTabLoad reads mappsorttab[mappfilenbr] after the last mapping pair matched.
  sh ../build.sh $WORK/build _pristine ; ./tabload_pristine
Graph labels {0,0,1,2} (duplicate label 0; neither graphBuild nor graphCheck rejects this),
mapping file "1\n0 5\n".
  pristine: parttab = 5 0 -1 -1   expected: 5 -1 -1 -1   FAIL   (vertex 1 gets a garbage part)
  patched (commit 0006): parttab = 5 -1 -1 -1   ok
ASan is silent on the stock library because mappsorttab and vertsorttab share one memAllocGroup
block (the stray cell is vertsorttab[0]). split/ proves the out-of-bounds index with the pristine
routine compiled with the two arrays in separate allocations (library_graph_map_io_split.c,
generated from the 7.0.17 source by the commands in the shell history, see split/):
  ==ERROR: AddressSanitizer: heap-buffer-overflow ... READ of size 4
    #0 SCOTCH_graphTabLoadSplit library_graph_map_io_split.c:163
  0x... is located 0 bytes after 8-byte region   (the one-entry mapping array)
With unique labels the stray read also happens but is harmless (vertsorttab[0].labl <= current label).
